Finish a Wine thread's exit when one of its pthread TSD destructors faults.

Without this, segv_handler() dereferences NULL thread data and the thread retries the fault forever, so the process
never exits. pthread_exit_wrapper() records the exiting thread, and the arm64 signal handlers send a fault in its TSD
destructors to warzag_exit_after_teardown_fault(), which clears the next TSD key and calls pthread_exit() again.
abort(), __builtin_trap() and unresolved faults of threads without Wine data stay fatal. Test: qa/n/exit-hang.sh.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (a change to Wine).

